thread:
elin: dropping a short thread on a focused dark-mode pass for the console. goal: reduce visual competition between metrics, code, and alerts. figma: https://www.figma.com/file/xyz/coalproof-theme

noah: saw the frames, nice restraint. one thing: sparkline + success-green sit too close. sparkline currently #9bd4a8 and success is #57d98b

tess: what if sparks become a cool slate instead of green? less 'traffic' feel. try #6f98b0

sam_frontend: put up a tiny preview branch: /deploy-preview/507. CSS vars I changed:
```
:root {
  --bg: #061019;
  --panel: #0b1114;
  --fg: #dbeaf2;
  --sparkline: #6f98b0;
  --accent: #cfae67;
  --muted: #8e9aa6;
}
```

kai_a11y: quick accessibility note: small caption text (11px) with --muted (#8e9aa6) on panel (#0b1114) is 3.7:1. body copy needs 4.5:1. solutions: raise to 12px, bold, or use #b1c5d6

elin: for speed let's bold captions (600) and revisit size in a follow-up. also chart lines in dark panels read thin at 1px. propose 1.5px and subtle border: rgba(219,231,238,0.05)

sam_frontend: updated chart defaults in preview: lineWidth 1.5, gridColor rgba(219,231,238,0.04). also swapped sparkline to #6f98b0 per tess

noah: syntax highlight question: functions are teal now which collides with sparkline. current code palette: keywords #cfae67, functions #6fc2b0, strings #d6a58d, comments #6e7b85

tess: i'd prefer functions shift closer to steel blue (#5f8ea0) so charts and code don't fight for attention. keep keywords warmish gold

kai_a11y: after moving functions to #5f8ea0, re-ran contrast checks. inline code on panel is 4.7:1, comments 4.2, captions (bolded) 4.5. good enough for now but track any copy shrinkage

theme-bot: scheduled a short internal compare: coalproof-vA (current) vs coalproof-vB (tweaks) for 36h with 40 internal users each. will post metrics (task clarity, click rates)

elin: thanks all. i'll open a PR with the vars + chart defaults. small follow-ups: revisit tooltip background (maybe raise alpha) and test heatmap gradient for low-value visibility

sam_frontend: note for heatmap: gradient proposal -> #041218 -> #153243 -> #5f8ea0 -> #cfe7ff. keeps lows very dark, highs readable

noah: perfect. short and tidy. thanks :white_check_mark:
